                <pb facs="0761" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/181 a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Elanco
                        Forwarding Corporation of New York</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Redondo</hi> which carries a cargo of flour and which was consigned to
                    Falmouth for orders, should now proceed to Reval and report to the
                    representative of the American Relief Administration who will issue the
                    necessary instructions for the discharge of this cargo.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Breckinridge Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
